{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/926487-the-guilds-in-modern-stygia","id":926487,"title":"The Guilds in Modern Stygia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-05T10:21:44-07:00","id":926487,"title":"The Guilds in Modern Stygia","content":"I'm reading the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-editio/posts/1619332\" target=\"_blank\">latest W20 writeups</a> and I was confused by this:<br /> <br /> &quot;The so-called Criminal Guilds traffic in Arcanoi that defies the Dictum Mortuum, and as such they\u2019re automatically on the wrong side of the law. Stygian authorities work very hard at justifying not aggressively outlawing these guilds - Spooks, Haunters, Proctors, Puppeteers and Monitors ...&quot;<br /> <br /> Wait, Monitors? Does Lifeweb have an art that violates the Dictum Mortuum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:00:36-07:00","id":926516,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'm under the impression the Monitor Guild is a Criminal Guild because of its potential to manipulate Fetters. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:29:07-07:00","id":926536,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's because of the fetters thing. If you can create new fetters, you can destroy them too. And that's why Lifeweb is criminalised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:38:54-07:00","id":926540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bphillips</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/926487-the-guilds-in-modern-stygia#post926487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-editio/posts/1619332\" target=\"_blank\">latest W20 writeups</a> and I was confused by this:<br /> <br /> &quot;The so-called Criminal Guilds traffic in Arcanoi that defies the Dictum Mortuum, and as such they\u2019re automatically on the wrong side of the law. Stygian authorities work very hard at justifying not aggressively outlawing these guilds - Spooks, Haunters, Proctors, Puppeteers and Monitors ...&quot;<br /> <br /> Wait, Monitors? Does Lifeweb have an art that violates the Dictum Mortuum?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do in Wr20 - Strand Channel, which allows a Monitor to speak through their Fetter, and use their Arcanoi as if they were at its location.<br /> <br /> Not only that, it's also the Guild's abuse of Lifeweb to screw with wraiths' connections to the living world - Fetters, Legacy, Memoriam... (Lifeweb in Wr20 primarily covers Fetters, but also covers a wraith's other connections to the Skinlands.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:28:26-07:00","id":991205,"title":"","content":"There's also that whole bit with the &quot;we tracked down and destroyed or severed a bunch of Fetters, barring a bunch of elder Wraiths from the Shadowlands&quot; thing that the Monitors are heavily implied to have facilitated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}